{"type":"user","message":{"role":"user","content":[{"type":"text","text":"This session is being continued from a previous conversation that ran out of context. The summary below covers the earlier portion of the conversation.\n\nSummary:\n1. Primary Request and Intent:\n   The user invoked a stitch task (Task ID 5342) to implement srd037-ln requirements R3.1 through R3.4 in the existing cmd/ln/main.go. The four requirements are:\n   - R3.1: `-f`/`--force` — remove existing destination files before creating the link\n   - R3.2: `-n`/`--no-dereference` — treat a destination that is a symlink to a directory as a regular file, rather than following it\n   - R3.3: `-i`/`--interactive` — prompt the user on stderr before removing an existing destination, with specific format `ln: replace 'DEST'? `, stdin reading, isatty check (decline if not terminal), and `-f`/`-i` last-flag-wins behavior\n   - R3.4: `-v`/`--verbose` — print the name of each link created to stdout\n\n   The task explicitly does NOT include R3.5 (backup `-b`) or R3.6 (suffix `-S`), even though the task title mentions \"backup and target directory modes.\" The non_goals in the SRD exclude `-t DIRECTORY` and `-T` flags.\n\n   Acceptance criteria: `go build` succeeds, `go vet` clean, all four R3.x requirements implemented, and previously implemented R1.x/R2.x functionality preserved.\n\n2. Key Technical Concepts:\n   - Go reimplementation of GNU `ln` (coreutils), verified against `gln` via differential testing\n   - SIGPIPE handler via `pkg/sys.InstallSIGPIPEHandler()`\n   - Hard links vs symbolic links\n   - `-f`/`-i` last-flag-wins pattern (GNU ln behavior)\n   - `os.Lstat` vs `os.Stat` for no-dereference behavior\n   - isatty check on stdin for interactive mode\n   - Function size limit: 40 lines max (E8)\n   - File size limit: 500 lines max (E9)\n   - No git commands (orchestrator manages git)\n   - Write all files before building (go_style_constitution implementation_strategy)\n\n3. Files and Code Sections:\n   - `docs/specs/software-requirements/srd037-ln.yaml`\n     - Full SRD for ln, read to understand requirements R3.1-R3.4\n     - Key R3.3 details: prompt format `ln: replace 'DEST'? `, read one line from stdin, 'y'/'Y' prefix to proceed, isatty check (decline if not terminal), -f/-i last-wins\n     - Key R3.4: verbose prints link name to stdout\n     - Non-goals: no -t DIRECTORY, -T, -L, -P flags\n   \n   - `cmd/ln/main.go` (existing, needs modification)\n     - Currently implements R1.1-R1.4, R2.1-R2.4 (hard links, symbolic links with -s/-r)\n     - Current `options` struct has only `symbolic bool` and `relative bool`\n     - Current `parseArgs` handles `--`, long flags, short flags, positional args\n     - Current `createLink` handles symbolic vs hard link creation with relative path computation\n     - Current `isDirectory` uses `os.Stat` (follows symlinks) — needs update for `-n`\n     - `run()` function dispatches based on target count and last-arg-is-directory\n     - Helper functions: `computeRelative`, `createHardLink`, `isDirectory`, `targetDirError`, `sysErrMsg`, `errnoMsg`\n     - Full existing code (257 lines) captured above in file read\n\n4. Errors and fixes:\n   - No errors encountered yet; work had not begun beyond reading files.\n\n5. Problem Solving:\n   - No implementation work started. Was in the planning/reading phase when summary was requested.\n\n6. All user messages:\n   - First message: A massive task specification including role definition, repository file listing, project context (vision, architecture, specifications, roadmap, analysis, requirement states), execution constitution, go style constitution, task description, shared protocols, and package contracts. The core request is to implement srd037-ln R3.1-R3.4 in cmd/ln/main.go.\n   - Second message: \"CRITICAL: Respond with TEXT ONLY. Do NOT call any tools.\" — requesting a detailed summary of the conversation.\n\n7. Pending Tasks:\n   - Implement `-f`/`--force` flag in cmd/ln/ma