{"type":"user","message":{"role":"user","content":[{"tool_use_id":"toolu_01UuQsBmJuByMcmMG9dGraQ9","type":"tool_result","content":[{"type":"text","text":"Perfect! I have all the information needed. Let me provide you with the findings:\n\n## Summary\n\nI found the terminal-related functions in your Go project. Here's what I discovered:\n\n### Dependencies\n**File:** `/private/var/folders/dl/cbns6zkx7txc7pt64b6cgzp40000gn/T/go-unix-utils-worktrees/5342/go.mod`\n\n- The project uses `golang.org/x/sys v0.44.0` (not `golang.org/x/term`, but `golang.org/x/sys`)\n\n### Terminal Functions in pkg/sys/\n**File:** `/private/var/folders/dl/cbns6zkx7txc7pt64b6cgzp40000gn/T/go-unix-utils-worktrees/5342/pkg/sys/terminal.go`\n\n**Function signatures:**\n1. `func IsTerminal(fd uintptr) bool`\n   - Checks if a file descriptor is a terminal by attempting to get the window size\n   - Returns `true` if the ioctl call succeeds, `false` otherwise\n   - Implementation uses `unix.IoctlGetWinsize()` with `unix.TIOCGWINSZ`\n\n2. `func TerminalWidth() (int, error)`\n   - Gets the terminal width in columns\n   - Uses `os.Stdout.Fd()` to get stdout's file descriptor\n   - Returns the column width or an error\n\n### Usage Pattern\nTo check if stdin is a terminal, you would use:\n```go\nIsTerminal(uintptr(os.Stdin.Fd()))  // returns bool\n```\n\nThe implementation leverages `golang.org/x/sys/unix` for Unix-specific terminal ioctl operations rather than a separate `golang.org/x/term` dependency."}]}]},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"64f379ca-8127-473c-b4f2-b8d36f5c5b6f","uuid":"1fb6b460-a87e-466c-885c-2d771dfbb878","timestamp":"2026-05-20T11:35:31.572Z","tool_use_result":{"status":"completed","prompt":"In this Go project, I need to find how to check if stdin is a terminal (isatty). Search in pkg/sys/ for any isatty, IsTerminal, or terminal-related functions. Also check if there's a golang.org/x/term or similar dependency in go.mod. Report the function signatures and file paths.","agentId":